{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon ECR enhanced scanning now surfaces image use status - AWS","context":"Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) enhanced scanning now provides information on how images are used on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) and Amazon Elastic Container Service (ECS). This includes the last used date, the number of clusters using the image, and the ARNs of the clusters. This data can help prioritize vulnerability remediation for actively used images. ECR enhanced scanning is an integration with Amazon Inspector, which scans container images for operating system and programming language package vulnerabilities. Users can now identify when an image was last used, the number of clusters using it, and which clusters are running it with ARNs using the ECR or Inspector consoles and APIs. ECR enhanced scanning updates the image use status continuously and is available to enhanced scanning customers at no additional cost in all AWS Commercial and AWS GovCloud (US) Regions where enhanced scanning is available. To get started with ECR enhanced scanning, visit the ECR documentation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/06/amazon-ecr-scanning-surfaces-image-status/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"aws-containers","skill_description":"Builds, deploys, debugs, and optimizes containerized workloads on Amazon EKS, ECS, Fargate, ECR, and Elastic Beanstalk. Covers EKS operations and add-ons; ECS task definitions, services, Exec, Express Mode, Managed Instances, and Action Logs; ECR repositories and lifecycle policies; and Elastic Beanstalk platforms plus Beanstalk Cluster Mode for running containerized applications on service-managed EKS compute. Use for container deployment, service selection, configuration, scaling, health, troubleshooting, image workflows, or deciding between Beanstalk-managed Cluster Mode and direct EKS. Should be used instead of relying on internal knowledge for these services.\n\nServices: ecs, ecr, eks, apprunner, beanstalk\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: containers, compute, kubernetes","skill_name":"aws-containers"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"amazon-ec2-image-builder","skill_description":"Creates and automates custom image builds with EC2 Image Builder - Linux, Windows, and macOS AMIs, and container images to ECR. Covers the build IAM role, Amazon-managed and custom components, image recipes, infrastructure and distribution configuration (launch templates, SSM parameters, other Regions), one-off builds, recurring scheduled pipelines for golden AMI automation and OS patching, custom image workflows, and diagnosing failed builds. Applies when creating, automating, or scheduling AMI or container image builds with Image Builder, or when debugging a failed build. Not for launching instances from existing AMIs, AMI lifecycle/retirement, or general EC2 fleet management.\n\nServices: imagebuilder, ec2, ecr, iam\nTasks: create, configure, deploy, debug\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: compute, containers\n*","skill_name":"amazon-ec2-image-builder"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"launching-ec2-instance-with-best-practices","skill_description":"Launches an EC2 instance with secure, cost-efficient defaults including AMI selection, burstable instance sizing, least-privilege IAM roles, hardened security groups, encrypted EBS volumes, and comprehensive tagging. Use when deploying new EC2 instances following AWS best practices for security and cost optimization.\n\nServices: ec2, iam, vpc, cloudwatch, ebs\nTasks: deploy, configure, secure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: compute\n*","skill_name":"launching-ec2-instance-with-best-practices"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up CIS EKS 5.1.1 benchmark control"}

