{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon EKS introduces enhanced network security policies - AWS","context":"Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) has introduced enhanced network security policies to improve the security posture for Kubernetes workloads and integrations with external destinations. These enhancements include the ability to centrally enforce network access filters across the entire cluster and leverage Domain Name System (DNS) based policies for securing egress traffic. EKS now supports Kubernetes NetworkPolicies in the Amazon VPC Container Network Interface (VPC CNI) plugin, enabling pod-to-pod communication segmentation at a namespace level. Cluster admins can now prevent unauthorized access to cluster-external resources using egress rules that filter traffic based on Fully Qualified Domain Names (FQDN). These new features are available in all commercial AWS Regions for new EKS clusters running Kubernetes version 1.29 or later, with support for existing clusters to follow. ClusterNetworkPolicy is available in all EKS cluster launch modes using VPC CNI v1.21.1 or later, while DNS-based policies are only supported in EKS Auto Mode-launched EC2 instances","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/12/amazon-eks-enhanced-network-security-policies/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"amazon-keyspaces","skill_description":"Provides authoritative compatibility checks, pricing estimates, connection troubleshooting, pre-warming guidance, and infrastructure mutations for Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra). Covers LWT/batch operations, secondary indexes, materialized views, capacity modes, TTL, PITR, CDC, auto-scaling, multi-region keyspaces, UDTs, nodetool diagnostics parsing, SQL-to-Cassandra migration, and Cassandra-to-Keyspaces migration scenarios. Agents frequently produce incomplete or incorrect answers about Keyspaces feature support without this skill loaded.\n\nServices: keyspaces, cassandra\nTasks: cost-estimation, migration-assessment, compatibility-check, data-modeling, create, modify\nPersona: developer, devops, architect, dba\nWorkload: nosql, wide-column-store, cassandra-migration\n*","skill_name":"amazon-keyspaces"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"creating-production-vpc-multi-az","skill_description":"Creates a production-ready VPC with public and private subnets across multiple Availability Zones, including internet gateway, NAT gateways, route tables, and security groups following AWS Well-Architected principles. Use when deploying multi-AZ VPC infrastructure with automatic CIDR planning and DNS resolution.\n\nServices: ec2, vpc\nTasks: create, configure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: networking\n*","skill_name":"creating-production-vpc-multi-az"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"configuring-vpc-endpoints-for-private-aws-service-access","skill_description":"Configures VPC endpoints (interface and gateway) for private AWS service access using AWS PrivateLink. Use when setting up secure private connectivity to S3, DynamoDB, and other AWS services without internet gateway, NAT device, or public IP addresses. Covers endpoint creation, security groups, route tables, and DNS configuration.\n\nServices: ec2, vpc, s3, dynamodb\nTasks: configure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: networking\n*","skill_name":"configuring-vpc-endpoints-for-private-aws-service-access"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS-6 supplementary EKS check"}

